# CODEOWNERS — automatic reviewer assignment for pinpredict/pre-commit-hooks
#
# Without this file nothing requests a reviewer, so every review has to be
# asked for by hand. GitHub's scheduled reminders also key off review requests.
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins; listing several owners requests all of
# them. GitHub never requests review from the PR's own author, so an owner who
# opens a PR simply drops out of that one. Last-match-wins is per FILE: a PR
# that touches two areas requests both lists.
#
# Owners are individual GitHub handles, never org teams. Every area has at
# least two, so nothing blocks on one person and a sole author's own PRs still
# get a reviewer.
#
# Shared pre-commit hooks every repo pins by rev. A hook change lands in every
# consumer on its next bump, so the platform pair reviews it. The Kafka topic
# grandfather list (pinpredict_hooks/kafka_legacy_topics.py) only ever
# shrinks; an addition to it is the thing this file exists to catch.
